# WinRM / Ansible on macOS

Before running ANY Ansible command that targets Windows hosts (WinRM), the following
environment variables MUST be set. They live in the project `.envrc` file and are
loaded automatically by direnv (`direnv allow`).

```bash
export OBJC_DISABLE_INITIALIZE_FORK_SAFETY=yes
export no_proxy=*
```

When using the Shell tool, always source `.envrc` (or export these vars) before
running `ansible`, `ansible-playbook`, or any `./bin/fz` command that targets
Windows hosts. Without these, WinRM connections will crash with
"A worker was found in a dead state".

Example:

```bash
cd /Users/joshc/develop/dotfile-vnext && source .envrc && source .venv/bin/activate && ansible ...
```
